Here is a complete, self-contained CUDA program for the GH200 (sm_90a) that
measures genuine co-residency of CTAs from two concurrently launched kernels on
the same SM. It records per-CTA start/stop times using `%globaltimer` and the SM
ID using `%smid`, and then post-processes the data on the host to find the peak
number of CTAs resident on any single SM at any instant.

